==English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|discernen}}, borrowed from {{bor|en|fro|discerner}}, from {{der|en|la|discernere||to separate, divide, distinguish, discern}}, from {{m|la|dis-||apart}} + {{m|la|cernere||to separate}}; see [[certain]].

===Pronunciation===
* {{rhymes|ɜː(ɹ)n|lang=en}}
''(modern pronunciation)''
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/dɪˈsɜːn/|lang=en}}
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|/dɪˈsɝn/|lang=en}}
* {{audio|en-us-discern.ogg|Audio (US)|lang=en}}

''(older pronunciation)''
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/dɪˈzɜːn/|lang=en}}
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|/dɪˈzɝn/|lang=en}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[detect]] with the [[sense]]s, especially with the [[eye]]s.
#* {{quote-book
|lang=en
|year=1875
|author=Jules Verne you are no HELP!
|title=The Survivors of the Chancellor
|chapter=1
|url=http://ebooks.adelaide.edu.au/v/verne/jules/v52sc/chapter1.html
|passage=Meanwhile the brig had altered her tack, and was moving slowly to the east. Three hours later and the keenest eye could not have '''discerned''' her top-sails above the horizon.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[perceive]], [[recognize]], or [[comprehend]] with the [[mind]]; to [[descry]].
#* {{quote-book
|lang=en
|year=1842
|author=Charles Dickens
|title=American Notes for General Circulation
|url=http://ebooks.adelaide.edu.au/d/dickens/charles/d54an/preface1.html
|passage=If they '''discern''' any evidences of wrong-going in any direction that I have indicated, they will acknowledge that I had reason in what I wrote. If they '''discern''' no such thing, they will consider me altogether mistaken.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[distinguish]] something as being [[different]] from something else; to [[differentiate]].
#* {{quote-book
|lang=en
|year=1651
|author=Thomas Hobbes
|title=Leviathan
|url=http://ebooks.adelaide.edu.au/h/hobbes/thomas/h68l/conclusion.html
|passage=The severity of judgement, they say, makes men censorious and unapt to pardon the errors and infirmities of other men: and on the other side, celerity of fancy makes the thoughts less steady than is necessary to '''discern''' exactly between right and wrong.}}
#: ''He was too young to '''discern''' right from wrong.''
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To [[perceive]] [[difference]]s.

